	"Name": "Japanese seasonal extendable windows",
	"Author": "Asterisk555",
	"TagLine": "Round extendable windows for Alternative Textures and content patcher",
	"Description": "_Description_\n\n*   Round extendable windows\n\n*   Optional file has a version using colours from DaisyNiko's earthy recolour so it's not so bright\n\n*   Alternative Textures and mobile compatible content patcher version available\n\n_Quick start instructions\n_\n\n1.  Skip these instructions if you're downloading the content patcher version, the instructions for that are in the \"Read Me\" inside the mod folder\n\n2.  Download one of the (AT)\n\n3.  Download and extract this mod and it's requirements into your mods folder (if you are confused check out [this guide](https://stardewvalleywiki.com/Modding:Player_Guide/Getting_Started#Getting_started) ).\n\n4.  Buy the paint bucket at Robin's shop to retexture items. There is a [video](https://youtu.be/OzCzEppsXVY)  on how to use the mod in-game.\n\n_Tips and tricks_\n\n*   The basic, boarded, and small window has retextures\n\n*   The basic window is the seasonal version and sometimes looks better with [window light removal](https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/10289) , while the small window has plain backgrounds which are not seasonal but look good with window light\n\n*   The boarded window has shoji screens, and the light is blocked so it looks more natural and like the screens are blocking the light\n\n_Recommended Mods_\n\n*   [Light Tweaks and Auto Fireplaces](https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/10223)\n\n*   Scenery in the DN version is from [DaisyNiko's Earthy recolour](https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/5255)\n\n*   [Japanese wallpapers and flooring](https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/12993)\n\n*   [Chests and minifridges as baskets](https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/12219)\n\n*   Industrial/Basic [extendable windows](https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/11807)\n\n*   [Bathroom Extension](https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/12404)",
